  "id": "COMPOUND:9771 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Ligelizumab may interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through a series of target relationships. Specifically, Ligelizumab is predicted to target Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Tatridin B and Quassin. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of the CDC2L1 kinase, indicating a potential pathway through which Ligelizumab may exert its effects. The scores from the predictions suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights the role of these enzymes in the regulation of CDC2L1, and the potential for Ligelizumab to modulate this pathway. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Ligelizumab may influence the activity of CDC2L1 through the targeting of its upstream regulators.",
